  {"subject":"maths","q":"The value of the definite integral ∫₀^π sin(x) dx is:","options":["0","1","2","π"],"correct":2,"explain":"∫₀^π sin(x)dx = [-cos(x)]₀^π = -cos(π)-(-cos(0)) = 1+1 = 2."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"If a square matrix A is singular, its determinant is:","options":["1","-1","0","Undefined"],"correct":2,"explain":"A matrix is called singular if and only if its determinant equals zero."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The number of real solutions of the equation sin(x) = 2 is:","options":["1","2","Infinite","0"],"correct":3,"explain":"Since sin(x) ranges only between -1 and 1, the equation sin(x)=2 has no real solutions."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The sum of an infinite geometric series with first term a and common ratio r (|r|<1) is:","options":["a/(1-r)","a/(1+r)","a·r","a+r"],"correct":0,"explain":"For an infinite geometric series with |r|<1, the sum converges to a/(1-r)."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The value of i² (where i is the imaginary unit) is:","options":["1","-1","i","-i"],"correct":1,"explain":"By definition, the imaginary unit i satisfies i² = -1."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The general solution of the equation cos(x) = 1 is:","options":["x = nπ","x = 2nπ","x = nπ/2","x = (2n+1)π/2"],"correct":1,"explain":"cos(x)=1 occurs at x = 0, 2π, 4π,... so the general solution is x = 2nπ, where n is an integer."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The distance between the points (0,0) and (3,4) is:","options":["3","4","5","7"],"correct":2,"explain":"Using the distance formula, √(3²+4²) = √25 = 5."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The derivative of ln(x) with respect to x is:","options":["x","1/x","ln(x)","e^x"],"correct":1,"explain":"The derivative of the natural logarithm function ln(x) is 1/x."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"If a fair die is thrown once, the probability of getting an even number is:","options":["1/6","1/3","1/2","2/3"],"correct":2,"explain":"There are 3 even numbers (2,4,6) out of 6 possible outcomes, giving a probability of 3/6 = 1/2."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The equation of a circle centered at the origin with radius r is:","options":["x + y = r","x² + y² = r","x² + y² = r²","xy = r²"],"correct":2,"explain":"The standard equation of a circle centered at the origin is x² + y² = r², where r is the radius."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The value of 0! (zero factorial) is:","options":["0","1","Undefined","-1"],"correct":1,"explain":"By mathematical convention, 0! is defined to equal 1."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The nth term of an arithmetic progression with first term a and common difference d is given by:","options":["a + nd","a + (n-1)d","a·d^(n-1)","(n-1)/d"],"correct":1,"explain":"The nth term formula for an AP is a + (n-1)d, where a is the first term and d is the common difference."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The value of tan(45°) is:","options":["0","1","√3","Undefined"],"correct":1,"explain":"tan(45°) = sin(45°)/cos(45°) = 1, since sine and cosine are equal at 45°."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"If f(x) = x³, the second derivative f''(x) is:","options":["3x²","6x","x²","6"],"correct":1,"explain":"f'(x) = 3x², and differentiating again gives f''(x) = 6x."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The number of ways to select r objects from n distinct objects, disregarding order, is denoted by:","options":["nPr","nCr","n!","n/r"],"correct":1,"explain":"The combination formula nCr represents the number of ways to choose r objects from n without regard to order."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The area of a triangle given its vertices' coordinates is most conveniently calculated using a:","options":["Trigonometric identity","Determinant formula","Quadratic formula","Binomial expansion"],"correct":1,"explain":"The area of a triangle from coordinate vertices is calculated using a 3x3 determinant formula divided by 2."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The value of loge(1) (natural log of 1) is:","options":["0","1","e","Undefined"],"correct":0,"explain":"Since e^0 = 1, the natural logarithm of 1 is 0."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"A function f(x) is continuous at a point x=a if the limit of f(x) as x approaches a equals:","options":["Zero","Infinity","f(a)","The derivative at a"],"correct":2,"explain":"Continuity at a point requires the limit of the function to equal the function's actual value at that point."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The slope of a horizontal line is:","options":["0","1","Undefined","-1"],"correct":0,"explain":"A horizontal line has no vertical change, giving it a slope of exactly 0."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The modulus of a complex number a + bi is given by:","options":["a + b","a - b","√(a² + b²)","a² + b²"],"correct":2,"explain":"The modulus (absolute value) of a complex number a+bi is calculated as √(a²+b²)."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The value of ∫ e^x dx is:","options":["e^x + C","x·e^x + C","e^x/x + C","ln(x) + C"],"correct":0,"explain":"The integral of e^x with respect to x is simply e^x + C, since e^x is its own antiderivative."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"If two lines are parallel, their slopes are:","options":["Equal","Negative reciprocals","Both zero","Undefined"],"correct":0,"explain":"Parallel lines never intersect and always have exactly equal slopes."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The maximum value of sin(x) for real x is:","options":["0","0.5","1","Undefined"],"correct":2,"explain":"The sine function oscillates between -1 and 1, so its maximum value is 1."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The rank of a 3×3 identity matrix is:","options":["1","2","3","0"],"correct":2,"explain":"An identity matrix always has full rank equal to its order, so a 3×3 identity matrix has rank 3."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The number of terms in the binomial expansion of (x+y)^n is:","options":["n","n-1","n+1","2n"],"correct":2,"explain":"The binomial expansion of (x+y)^n always has exactly (n+1) terms."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"Standard deviation is a statistical measure of:","options":["Central tendency","Dispersion (spread of data)","Probability","Correlation"],"correct":1,"explain":"Standard deviation measures how spread out data values are from the mean, i.e., dispersion."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"If P(A) = 0.4 and P(B) = 0.5, and A and B are mutually exclusive events, then P(A∪B) is:","options":["0.2","0.7","0.9","1.0"],"correct":2,"explain":"For mutually exclusive events, P(A∪B) = P(A) + P(B) = 0.4 + 0.5 = 0.9."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The vertex form of a parabola's equation is especially useful for directly identifying its:","options":["Roots only","Vertex coordinates","Axis of symmetry only","y-intercept"],"correct":1,"explain":"The vertex form y = a(x-h)² + k directly reveals the vertex coordinates (h,k) of the parabola."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The value of sec(0°) is:","options":["0","1","-1","Undefined"],"correct":1,"explain":"sec(0°) = 1/cos(0°) = 1/1 = 1."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The dot product of two perpendicular (orthogonal) vectors is:","options":["1","-1","0","Equal to their magnitudes"],"correct":2,"explain":"The dot product of two perpendicular vectors is always zero, since cos(90°) = 0."},
  {"subject":"maths","q":"The value of cot(90°) is:","options":["0","1","Undefined","-1"],"correct":0,"explain":"cot(90°) = cos(90°)/sin(90°) = 0/1 = 0."}
